<title>RUSSIA: LUKoil, ARCO to sign Moscow deal.</title>
<headline>LUKoil, ARCO to sign Moscow deal.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's LUKoil and Atlantic Richfield Co (ARCO) of the United States will sign a cooperation deal on Thursday in Moscow, a LUKoil spokesman said.</p>
<p>Dmitry Dolgov did not say what the agreement would entail.</p>
<p>ARCO owns about eight percent of LUKoil's total equity, acquired through purchases of the company's convertible bonds in September 1995 and last April.</p>
<p>The two companies signed a cooperation agreement in March to jointly develop oil and gas projects in the former Soviet Union which could need up to $3 billion in financing over a decade.</p>
<p>LUKoil is Russia's largest oil producer.</p>
<p>-- Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
